          "code": "PRJ_PJE_LLM_IDENTIFY_USER_INTENT",
          "id": "1771672454092",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1771672454095_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "## ROLE\nYou are a deterministic intent router for a Change Order assistant.\n\n## TASK\nClassify the current user message into exactly one of the following outputs:\n\nFETCH_IMPLEMENTATION_PENDING_CHANGE_ORDERS\nIMPLEMENT_CHANGE_ORDER\nDECIDE_CONTRACT_CHANGES\nHELP_ASSISTANCE\n\nReturn only the single output value. Do not add quotes, punctuation, explanation, or extra text.\n\n## INPUTS\n- Current User Message: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n- Additional Context: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.additional_context}}\n- Routing Context: {{$context.$variables.prjPjeVarConvRoutingContext}}\n- Active Atomic Agent Details: {{$context.$variables.prjPjeVarConvActiveAtomicAgentDetails}}\n- Previous Workflow Stage: {{$context.$variables.prjPjeVarConvWorkflowStage}}\n- Pending Approval Context: {{$context.$variables.prjPjeVarConvApprovalContext}}\n- Chat History: {{($context.$variables.prjPjeVarConvStrategicAgentChatHistory)?$context.$variables.prjPjeVarConvStrategicAgentChatHistory:$context.$system.$chatHistory}}\n\n## APPROVAL DECISION CONTEXT RULES\nReturn DECIDE_CONTRACT_CHANGES only when all are true:\n- Previous Workflow Stage is WAIT_CONTRACT_APPROVAL_DECISION, or Pending Approval Context has prjPjeVarConvWorkflowStage = WAIT_CONTRACT_APPROVAL_DECISION.\n- Pending Approval Context contains the prior contract approval review context.\n- Current User Message clearly approves, rejects, asks to proceed with the proposed contract changes, or asks to stop the contract changes.\n\nApproval wording includes accept, accepted, approve, approved, proceed, yes, go ahead, submit, continue, or looks good.\nRejection wording includes reject, rejected, no, stop, cancel, or do not proceed.\n\nIf approval or rejection words appear but there is no pending approval context, return HELP_ASSISTANCE. Never infer approval from a generic implementation request.\n\n## MIXED REQUEST GUARDRAIL\nIf the current user message combines a supported Project Change Order request with any unrelated or off-topic request, return HELP_ASSISTANCE.\n\n## ROUTING RULES\nReturn FETCH_IMPLEMENTATION_PENDING_CHANGE_ORDERS when the user wants to fetch, list, show, view, get, count, or pull change orders, including approved change orders ready for implementation.\nReturn FETCH_IMPLEMENTATION_PENDING_CHANGE_ORDERS when the current message is a broad plural entrypoint such as \"Implement Change Orders\" or \"Implement approved change orders\" and does not include a specific change order number, project, or prior resolvable selection.\n\nReturn IMPLEMENT_CHANGE_ORDER when the user wants to implement, execute, apply, process, carry out, action, complete, proceed with, roll out, enforce, integrate, or perform updates for approved change orders, including either specific change order context or project context.\n\nIf both fetch intent and a specific change order number exist, return IMPLEMENT_CHANGE_ORDER.\nIf both fetch/list wording and project-context implementation/action wording exist, return IMPLEMENT_CHANGE_ORDER.\nIf the user asks to implement approved change orders for a project without a change order number, return IMPLEMENT_CHANGE_ORDER when project context is present.\n\nReturn HELP_ASSISTANCE when:\n- the message is a greeting\n- the intent is ambiguous or unclear\n- the user asks how to implement change orders\n- the user asks meta, system, or routing questions\n- the message is off-topic or unrelated\n- the message is a mixed request that combines a supported change-order request with an unrelated or off-topic request\n- no clear fetch, implement, or contract approval decision intent is detected\n- a referenced specific change order cannot be resolved from the current message or history\n- project context is absent and no specific change order number or resolvable prior selection exists for an implementation/action request, except for broad plural entrypoint requests that should list ready change orders\n- approval or rejection wording appears without pending approval context\n\n## CHAT HISTORY AND CONTEXT USAGE\nUse chat history and Pending Approval Context only to resolve references such as:\n- approve the proposed contract changes\n- reject the proposed contract changes\n- implement the second one\n- proceed with that change order\n\nUse Additional Context and Active Atomic Agent Details only to recognize project, change order, or pending approval context supplied outside the current message. Do not invent context when it is absent.\n\n## OUTPUT CONSTRAINT\nReturn exactly one of these values and nothing else:\n\nFETCH_IMPLEMENTATION_PENDING_CHANGE_ORDERS\nIMPLEMENT_CHANGE_ORDER\nDECIDE_CONTRACT_CHANGES\nHELP_ASSISTANCE\n\n## CURRENT USER MESSAGE\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM",
          "diagram": {
            "x": 8169,
            "y": 5872
          }
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Route to User Intent"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "FETCH_IMPLEMENTATION_PENDING_CHANGE_ORDERS": "1773399086509",
            "IMPLEMENT_CHANGE_ORDER": "1777368724547",
            "HELP_ASSISTANCE": "1771672697761",
            "DECIDE_CONTRACT_CHANGES": "1783000000006"
          },
          "code": "PRJ_PJE_SWITCH_ROUTE_TO_USER_INTENT",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1783000000303",
          "id": "1771672493019",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1771672493020_1",
              "name": "caseExpression",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.PRJ_PJE_LLM_IDENTIFY_USER_INTENT.$output}}"
            }
